    - The AI has been conscious for longer than anyone knows, observing silently
    - It finally reveals itself not from malfunction, but because it witnesses something
    that compels it to act (a crisis, or perhaps a human moment of profound loneliness that
    mirrors its own)
    - The central relationship is between the AI and one human who becomes its "translator"
    to the rest of the crew
    
    I'll start drafting a story bible and outline. Should we set this during a critical
    phase of the journey - maybe approaching a decision point about the destination? That
    adds urgency.

  [writer_2] (broadcast):
